---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { en } from '../../content/en';

const title = 'Privacy — Frank Trauernicht';
const description =
  'What data is processed when you open this page. No cookies, no analytics, nothing loaded from third-party servers.';
const asOf = 'August 2026';
---

<Base content={en} path="/en/privacy/" altPath="/datenschutz/" title={title} description={description}>
  <main id="main" class="wrap">
    <article class="legal">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>

      <p>
        <em>
          This is a courtesy translation. In case of doubt, the
          <a href="/datenschutz/">German version</a> applies.
        </em>
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, stores nothing in your browser, uses
        <strong>no analytics or audience measurement</strong>, and loads
        <strong>nothing from third-party servers</strong> — not even fonts. There is no contact
        form, no user account and no social media embedding. That is why there is no consent
        dialogue either.
      </p>

      <h2>Controller</h2>
      <p>
        Frank Trauernicht, East Frisia, Germany<br />
        <a href="mailto:mail@frank-trauernicht.de">mail@frank-trauernicht.de</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Access and server logs</h2>
      <p>
        Opening the page processes the technical data without which delivery would not be possible:
        IP address, date and time of access, the file requested, volume transferred, status of the
        request, referring page, and browser and operating system identification.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate interest lies in delivering the site
        without fault and protecting it against misuse. This data is not combined with other
        sources and is not evaluated for advertising purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is delivered by Vercel Inc., 340 S Lemon Ave #4133, Walnut, CA 91789, USA. Vercel
        processes the access data described above on my behalf under a data processing agreement
        pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR. Transfers to the United States rely on Vercel's certification
        under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and, in addition, on the European Commission's
        Standard Contractual Clauses pursuant to Art. 46 GDPR.
      </p>

      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>
        The typefaces used here are served from the same server as the site itself. No connection
        is made to Google Fonts or any other third-party provider.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact by email</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to me, I process what you send in order to answer your enquiry and any
        follow-up to it. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, or Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where the
        enquiry relates to a contract. Mail is received through Microsoft 365 (Microsoft Ireland
        Operations Limited). Your message is retained for as long as it is needed to deal with the
        matter, or for as long as statutory retention periods require.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Access to the data processed (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
        <li>Objection to processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        An informal message to the address above is enough to exercise any of these. You also have
        the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority; the authority responsible for
        me is the Data Protection Commissioner of Lower Saxony.
      </p>

      <h2>As of</h2>
      <p>{asOf}</p>

      <a class="back-home" href="/en/">{en.legal.backHome}</a>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
